# The one file you edit (docs/INSTALL-CONTAINER.md). Compose does not read it by itself (it only reads a file called .env): always say
#   docker compose --env-file vedette.env up -d        (or podman compose --env-file vedette.env up -d)
#
# 1. The address of THIS machine on which the web page is served (a LAN address, or 127.0.0.1 to try it from this machine only).
VEDETTE_BIND_IP=
# 2. The name or address you type in the browser, comma separated; the box refuses any other (421) and puts them in its certificate.
VEDETTE_HOSTS=
#
# 3. The images of the release, by digest. A release fills these three lines and signs this file; in the repository they are empty on
# purpose, so a copy taken from the repository starts nothing. To try a local build, set them to your own images.
VEDETTE_CORE_IMAGE=
VEDETTE_SENSOR_IMAGE=
VEDETTE_SCAN_IMAGE=
